%% Circular terms (GLP-Spec glp.tex, "Circular terms", GLP-ICLP-2026 main;
%% Audit Finding 1, Grassroots-Audit #31).  The unit clause p(f(X?), X) and the
%% goal p(Y, Y?) have the writer mgu {Y := f(X?), X := Y?}, whose pair
%% completion would assign Y? a term in which Y? occurs: cGLP has no such
%% Reduce, so the terms of a cGLP run are finite.  "An implementation of GLP
%% makes no occurs check ... An implementation thus takes a step cGLP does not
%% have, and builds a circular term."  The program is well-typed (TGLP,
%% "Soundness of Well-Typing": well-typing does not exclude the cyclic writer
%% mgu).  Harness A44 holds the implementation to that sentence on the cyclic
%% goal, and to cGLP on the two acyclic controls, p(Y, a) and p(Y, Z?).

T ::= a ; f(T).

procedure p(T, T?).
p(f(X?), X).
